\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{One site for each cell}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{A [based cochain](fdip-00SH) assigns one fiber value to
each cell. At a vertex the direction sets of the based cells
index #{2^n} components, the same count as in the Pauli spin
space. The operator #{\extd+\extdag} joins cells whose degrees
differ by one. Doubling each period provides a different site
for every direction set and base vertex. Can a choice of phase
turn the two incidence signs into the forward and backward
staggered signs?}
